<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Emberfall.Tools.CollectionMigrate — ADR-0009 ruling 3, as a command.

    Each deck inherits its character's class pairing; the characters are then dropped. Local JSON
    and Postgres, run independently.

    A TOOL AND NOT A SHIM, which is the ruling. The greenfield rule is "conform the content, do not
    add back-compat"; this conversion is its one deliberate exception and is one-shot, so nothing in
    the shipped reader knows about the old shape. CollectionJson.ReadDecks therefore REQUIRES the
    pairing and throws on a file written before 2026-09-04 — deliberately, so a missed migration is
    a loud read error rather than a roster of decks that quietly defaulted to NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL and
    became illegal. That loudness is only defensible because this exists to run.

    NO REFERENCE TO Emberfall.Core.Collection, AND THAT IS THE POINT. This reads and writes the
    legacy shape, which that assembly's reader is built to refuse. Coupling them would either make
    the tool unable to open the files it exists for, or force a back-compat path back into the
    shipped reader — the exact thing the ruling avoids. It works in raw JSON instead, which also
    makes it lossless for fields added after it was written.

    RETIREMENT TRIGGER: delete this project, its solution entry, CollectionPaths.CharactersFileName
    and CollectionPaths.Characters once no device and no database still carries a pre-ADR-0009
    decks.json. Those two helpers exist only for this tool and carry the same marker.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>12</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <AssemblyName>Emberfall.Tools.CollectionMigrate</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Emberfall.Tools.CollectionMigrate</RootNamespace>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" Version="9.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
